        "title": "Free Monads in Practice",
        "abstract": "Free Monads are an alternative to the Monad Transformer design pattern. Using free monads, a programmer can create flexible, extensible programs by assembling larger monads from primitive ones without the static, inflexible designs of monad transformers.",
